<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110257" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φᾱνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (
			contr.
		 fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαεινός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>light, bright,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Parm.
				8.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
			</span></i> Com.<i><span class="en">
				93
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμα φανοτάτῳ τινὶ πυρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phlb.</u>
					16c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα ὡς φανότατον ᾖ τὸ ἔσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					10.7
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φ.</span>
			<i>brightness, light,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρέφειν πρὸς τὸ φ. ἐκ τοῦ σκοτώδους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					518c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				478c
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φανά τε καὶ καλά</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				506d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Po.</u>
				2.45
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φανότατος ἀήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					18(2).285
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς φανοτάτοις θεῶν Ἡλίῳ καὶ
					Σελήνῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					10.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of garments,
				<i>washed clean,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλαῖνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					845
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σισύρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					347
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>bright, joyous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαναῖς ἐν εὐφροσύναις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					538
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. βίον διάγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					256d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>conspicuous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλλόγιμος καὶ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					197a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νῶς</span>
			<i>clearly</i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φανότερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					4.145b
				</span></i>
			; 
				Sup.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φανότατα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				44
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φᾶνος, ὁ</span> (properisp., cf.
				Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.175
			</span></i>), name of a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συκοφάντης,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1256
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
